kosha rated-power

  -- the maximum continuous power a motor / actuator can deliver at a joint
  -- a physical limit of the stepper or servo motor
  --
  -- P = τ · ω  (torque times angular velocity)
  -- both torque and speed limits must be checked — a motor can be within
  -- torque rating but exceed power rating at high speed, or vice versa
  --
  -- in the chala-apeksha model:
  --   rated-power is defined at the joint's actuator (chala-apeksha frame)
  --   the actual power required = required-torque × actual-angular-velocity
  --   where required-torque includes the chala-apeksha coupling terms
  --
  -- motor-check tantra checks both rated-torque and rated-power:
  --   margin-power = rated-power - required-power
  --   a joint can fail either the torque check OR the power check or both

  "subanta-swarupa"
  "domain-robotics-sthita kinematic-chain-yukta"
  "shakti-abheda"
  "joint-yukta"
  "watt-matra"
  "seema-sthita"
  "chala-apeksha-sthita"

shabda rated-power, power-rating, max-power / the-maximum-power-the-motor-at-a-joint-can-deliver

